A||||2||Galen||'DIS' question .. ||||5||
Z||000000||Galen||10-15-2001||10:51 AM||||I recently noticed my POS 87 engine has devolped a leak, its a 87 2.5 Duke auto.. it appears to be leaking from around the DIS block.. what could be leaking and what would cause this?<P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||10-15-2001||10:54 AM||||It is probably the O-ring around the crank position sensor that is leaking.  Carefully remove the DIS coils, and the the PIM and its mounting plate to remove the crank sensor and replace its o-ring.  If the CPS is cracked or shows signs of wear replace it.  theogre has a good DIS article in his cave, you might want to check it out for more info and cautions about the DIS system.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-15-2001||07:24 PM||||Yup... CPS...<P>Don't need to take the brick apart. just take out the 3 bolts that hold the aluminum base to the engine. Much easier than messig with the coils and PIM on car.<P>Just replace the sensor. As old as it is... it's fairly cheap and not worth second guessing.<P>Clean the rest up good whitle it's out.<P>Don't forget to put thread sealer on the indicated bolts or they will leak oil.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
